 "grip": {
  "what": "Grip_R: local rotations of the right-hand finger bones only (Index/Middle/Ring/Pinky 1-3 curled 20/34/24 deg toward the palm, Thumb 1-3 closing over the shank 35/15/15 deg). Checked on the mesh: 36 of 320 finger vertices within 4 mm of the shank, deepest overlap 3.3 mm (a tight grip, no visible gap or slipping).",
  "why_a_layer": "every shared clip keys all 65 bones including the fingers (Walk_v04 up to 20 deg, Idle_Stand_v04 15 deg, Cop_ShakeFist_v02 84 deg), so a grip baked into the mesh would break; the override layer replaces only the right-hand finger rotations and keeps everything else of the base clip",
  "clip": "Animations_v01/MECHANIC_W86_Grip_R_v01.fbx, take Grip_R, 2 frames (constant), loop",
  "unity_setup": [
   "AvatarMask \"Mechanic_HandR_Grip.mask\" (Generic: Transform mask): import the skeleton from the mechanic FBX, untick everything, tick only the transforms listed in keyed_bones (mixamorig:RightHand children).",
   "Animator layer \"HandGrip_R\" as the LAST layer: blending Override, weight 1, mask Mechanic_HandR_Grip, one state playing Grip_R (loop) with no transitions.",
   "Leave NpcHeldProps off the mechanic. The Grip_R layer also covers the mechanic clips (they already hold the grip).",
   "Alternative without a layer: a LateUpdate script that sets these transforms to the Grip_R clip pose after the Animator (read the values from the clip, not from Blender quaternions: the FBX import converts axes)."
  ],
